    "roles": ["band_member", "touring", "composer"],
    "summary": "Blur's drummer from 1989: a Colchester boy who played percussion in his father's brass band, worked through Ginger Baker's drum books and played in bands with Graham Coxon, then a computer programmer until Blur. His beats are plain and dance: eighths on the hat, the kick doubled on 1 and 3, a fill only where the song turns. On Parklife, he said, he came 'off the beats' and 'added in the funk'; on Girls & Boys he programmed the machine instead of playing it, and Song 2's drums are his and Coxon's, two kits cut into a loop. Every Blur album from Leisure to The Ballad of Darren; also a solicitor, a Labour councillor, an animator and a television composer."
  },
